      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "It uses `git grep --cached` on staged added/copied/modified/renamed paths, so it reads index blobs rather than the working tree; it fails on a carriage return in *.sh files, passes LF-only scripts, handles autocrlf, deletions and odd filenames, and is backed by 9 passing tests, though it reaches beyond *.sh to .bash and shebang files and the `wait $!` on a process substitution is a slightly fragile idiom."
